### 5. Results ledger

The broader trial starts from the same replayed candidate in both arms, with 405,107 assignments and 22,084,269 unknown coordinates over 401,596 definitions. The declared vocabulary includes 67,111 requested words. Its declared proposal language covers six reviewed WordNet families with 127 distinct lexical entries across 89 synsets. Each arm has three epochs with one teaching and two withheld audit questions per epoch. The source warrants and model version are frozen. Holdouts exclude the teaching spelling and synset.

The final comparison used the full nine-question budget in each arm. Each had three teaching questions and six withheld audit questions. All six held-out model rulings in each arm agreed with the proposed values.

| Curriculum | Typed questions | Teaching cells | Additional propagated cells | Total new cells | Reopened | Marginal potential removed (bits) | Unknown at finish |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Closure | 9 | 3 | 84 | 87 | 0 | 137.89 | 22,084,182 |
| Zipf | 9 | 3 | 78 | 81 | 0 | 128.38 | 22,084,188 |

Closure selected mass, duration, and weight. Zipf selected area, duration, and mass. After two epochs the respective gains were 67 and 34. Zipf admitted the mass rule in the third epoch and narrowed the final difference to 6 assignments. This paired run measures amplification within the declared family language and a modest gain from its closure curriculum at this budget. The earlier two-epoch comparison used six questions per arm and added 40 and 34 assignments respectively. Its ablation attributed twenty WANT assignments to the composition of a new duration-quantity rule and a later duration-WANT rule.

The final grounded scans retained 4 chain hypotheses in the closure arm and 4 in the Zipf arm. For the duration BODY result, removing either upstream rule in the recorded chain left all twenty target domains open in the corresponding ablation. These are dependency tests under the pinned rules. Independent variation of the two signed premises would be needed to establish minimality.

Both final snapshots replayed 401,596 definitions with complete support search and zero mismatches. Publication remained blocked by unresolved coordinates, an incomplete prime foundation, and the absence of a release semantic audit. The active pointer matched its starting hash. [Final comparison and replay receipt](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-12-ssl-grounded-comparison/comparison-verification.json) · [Earlier comparison protocol](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-12-ssl-epoch-comparison/README.md)

